# Where the FastAPI backend is. Read at build time by Vite.
#
# 8000, the same as the backoffice and the seller's cabinet, because there is
# one backend and it listens there. This said 8001 on the assumption that the
# customer app ran a dev server of its own on 8000 — it does not: the customer
# app is the Android and iOS build, and it talks to this same 8000. The
# default in `src/api/client.ts` said 8001 too, so a courier opening the PWA
# with no `.env` reached nothing at all.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
